    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="0705" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg691"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.30 Missions/12–1544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-15T21:00:00-04:00">December 15,
                            1944—9 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1930. Fernández expresses greatest satisfaction over our willingness to send a
                    naval mission to Chile and the President expresses satisfaction with the
                    proposal to send first a Rear Admiral here to make a survey to determine amount
                    of personnel, et cetera. A formal request for the mission will be conveyed to
                    the Department by Ambassador Mora.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
